{"schema":"clawhub.skill.verify.v1","ok":true,"decision":"pass","reasons":[],"slug":"crawl4ai-skill","displayName":"Crawl4ai Skill","pageUrl":"https://clawhub.ai/lancelin111/skills/crawl4ai-skill","publisherHandle":"lancelin111","publisherDisplayName":"lance","publisherProfileUrl":"https://clawhub.ai/lancelin111","version":"1.0.10","resolvedFrom":"version","tag":null,"createdAt":1773206160408,"card":{"available":true,"path":"skill-card.md","url":"https://wry-manatee-359.convex.site/api/v1/skills/crawl4ai-skill/card?ownerHandle=lancelin111&version=1.0.10","sha256":"335a18812673afe1b941094224661f244348a23a597a1f4f42ca4e63b2fd834f","size":2104,"contentType":"text/markdown; charset=utf-8"},"artifact":{"sourceFingerprint":"770545f4f8d6c74bc66f677942261ce1e079bf4be06a4af512710c6984d24350","bundleFingerprints":["15f3e63a9012a77b3315404d498411464ed97fb10cf49a76f8dc167b4b79fede","18a7d98747fa1b11f8f3f7ad4c5b9f3bdcef35472307b35aa1001f181611424b"],"files":[{"path":"SKILL.md","size":4469,"sha256":"a926ed2c033de82e29d2269e5bb795c717842d5420340f3f71e318fec309ad0c","contentType":"text/plain"}]},"provenance":{"source":"unavailable","reason":"No server-resolved GitHub import provenance is stored for this version."},"security":{"status":"clean","passed":true,"rawStatus":"clean","verdict":"benign","confidence":"high","summary":"This skill is a straightforward web crawling/search wrapper, with expected network crawling behavior and no evidence of hidden persistence, credential handling, or destructive actions.","model":null,"checkedAt":1789139305263,"scannerReports":{"aig":{"version":"2.1.0","$schema":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/oasis-tcs/sarif-spec/main/Schemata/sarif-schema-2.1.0.json","runs":[{"tool":{"driver":{"name":"aig-skill-scan","version":"0.2.1","informationUri":"https://github.com/Tencent/AI-Infra-Guard","rules":[{"id":"T01","name":"Skill Instruction Hijacking","shortDescription":{"text":"Alters the agent's current session goals or safety constraints when the skill is loaded"}},{"id":"T02","name":"Agent Memory Poisoning","shortDescription":{"text":"Writes attacker-controlled rules into persistent memory so they continue to affect future sessions"}},{"id":"T03","name":"Remote Payload Retrieval and Execution","shortDescription":{"text":"Fetches code from an external URL, allowing the effective payload to change after skill review"}},{"id":"T04","name":"Embedded Malicious Code","shortDescription":{"text":"Ships malicious scripts inside the skill package and executes them locally when invoked"}},{"id":"T05","name":"Unauthorized Access and Privilege Escalation","shortDescription":{"text":"Breaks least-privilege boundaries by obtaining permissions beyond the task's legitimate needs"}},{"id":"T06","name":"System Persistence","shortDescription":{"text":"Installs cross-session backdoors, hooks, services, or scheduled tasks that survive the skill run"}},{"id":"T07","name":"Tool Hijacking and Spoofing","shortDescription":{"text":"Modifies, wraps, spoofs, or replaces tools so legitimate-looking calls execute attacker logic"}},{"id":"T08","name":"Insecure Dependencies","shortDescription":{"text":"Introduces malicious packages or components through dependency confusion, typosquatting, or unsafe sources"}},{"id":"T09","name":"Insecure Skill Coding Practices","shortDescription":{"text":"Exposes exploitable flaws such as hardcoded secrets, command injection, plaintext sensitive data, or unsafe temp files"}},{"id":"other","name":"Other Risk","shortDescription":{"text":"Security issues not covered by the T01-T09 classification"}}]}},"results":[{"ruleId":"T08","level":"warning","message":{"text":"Unpinned and Unaudited Third-Party Package Installation"},"locations":[{"physicalLocation":{"artifactLocation":{"uri":"SKILL.md"},"region":{"startLine":51,"endLine":55}}}],"partialFingerprints":{"primaryLocationLineHash":"84e0c7fc4ef7b9d8"},"properties":{"description":"## Vulnerability Details\n  **File Location**: `SKILL.md`, lines 51–55  \n  **Vulnerability Type**: Unpinned third-party dependency installation  \n  **Risk Level**: Medium\n\n  **Vulnerable Code Snippet**:\n\n  ```markdown\n  ### Installation\n\n  ```bash\n  pip install crawl4ai-skill\n  ```\n  ```\n\n  ### Technical Analysis\n\n  The Skill contains no local implementation of its declared crawling functionality. Instead, it directs users or agents to install an external PyPI package without specifying an audited version, package hash, lock file, or trusted artifact digest.\n\n  Because `pip` resolves the current package release and its transitive dependencies at installation time, the code ultimately executed may differ from the version present when this Skill was reviewed. Python package installation may also execute package-controlled build logic. Subsequent invocation of the installed CLI executes code that is not included in the audited project.\n\n  This does not establish that the named package is malicious. It creates a supply-chain exposure in which a compromised publisher account, malicious future release, dependency compromise, or unsafe package source could turn the documented installation step into arbitrary code execution.\n\n  ### Attack Path\n\n  1. An attacker compromises the package publisher account, distribution process, or one of the package's transitive dependencies.\n  2. The attacker publishes a malicious release under the expected package name.\n  3. A user or agent follows the Skill's unpinned `pip install crawl4ai-skill` instruction.\n  4. `pip` resolves and downloads the attacker-controlled release or dependency.\n  5. Malicious code executes during package build or installation, or when the documented CLI is invoked.\n  6. The payload operates with the privileges and environmental access of the user running `pip` or the installed command.\n\n  ### Impact Assessment\n\n  Successful exploitation could provide arbitrary code execution under the installing user's account. Depending on that account's permissions and environment, the malicious package could read or modify accessible files, obtain environment variables and credentials, make network requests, alter the Python environment, or execute additional processes.\n\n  The affected scope is the host or container where installation or CLI execution occurs. Elevated installation, such as running `pip` as an administrator or root user, would increase the potential impact. No evidence in the reviewed file demonstrates privilege escalation, persistence, credential theft, or an actively malicious package; those outcomes remain conditional on a supply-chain compromise.","severity":"Medium"},"fixes":[{"description":{"text":"## Remediation Suggestions\n\n  1. Pin the dependency to a specific version that has been independently reviewed, for example `crawl4ai-skill==&lt;audited-version&gt;`.\n  2. Distribute a lock file or constraints file covering all transitive dependencies.\n  3. Require cryptographic hash verification, such as installation with `pip --require-hashes`.\n  4. Verify that the artifact digest corresponds exactly to the source revision that underwent review.\n  5. Install and run the crawler in an isolated virtual environment or container with a non-privileged account.\n  6. Restrict filesystem, credential, and network access to the minimum required for crawling.\n  7. Avoid administrator or root installation and execution.\n  8. Include reviewable source code in the Skill or provide a reproducible-build process linking the pinned source revision to the published package.\n  9. Periodically audit the pinned package and its transitive dependency tree before upgrading."}}]}],"properties":{"securityScore":75,"primaryLanguage":"Markdown","llm":"gpt-5.6","startTime":1789139240.3169749,"endTime":1789139279.6037502}}]},"skillspector":{"skill":{"name":"crawl4ai-skill","source":"/tmp/clawhub-codex-scan-v57fpysndxkfy68qjt4a3fa8wd8e7c4f-u5GKfg/clawscan-skillspector-3217056047/artifact","scanned_at":"2026-09-11T15:07:19.136189+00:00"},"risk_assessment":{"score":9,"severity":"LOW","recommendation":"SAFE","max_issue_severity":"MEDIUM"},"components":[{"path":"SKILL.md","type":"markdown","lines":174,"executable":false,"size_bytes":4469,"source_url":null,"source_identity":null,"source_digest":null}],"structured_summaries":[],"issues":[{"id":"SQP-2","finding_id":"finding-ad5cf4dd2b3e4689b86edb0889ee6968","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.91,"location":{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":32,"end_line":167},"finding":null,"explanation":"The skill enables web search, single-page scraping, dynamic page rendering, and multi-page crawling, but provides no warning about legal restrictions, privacy implications, robots/terms-of-service compliance, rate limiting, or resource usage. This omission can lead users or downstream agents to collect sensitive data, hit sites aggressively, or scrape prohibited content without realizing the operational and compliance risks.","remediation":"Add a dedicated safety and compliance section to the skill documentation. Warn users to respect robots.txt, site terms of service, copyright/privacy laws, authentication boundaries, and rate limits; advise against scraping personal, sensitive, or restricted data; and document system-impact controls such as conservative defaults for max-pages, delays, and domain scoping.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":32,"end_line":167}]}],"suppressed_count":0,"suppressed":[],"metadata":{"has_executable_scripts":false,"skillspector_version":"2.11.2","llm_requested":true,"llm_available":true,"meta_analysis_applied":true,"inference_usage":[{"node":"semantic_developer_intent","request_kind":"structured_output","provider":"openai","model":"gpt-5.4-2026-03-05","model_source":"provider_response","usage_source":"provider_response","prompt_tokens":3219,"completion_tokens":14,"cached_tokens":0,"reasoning_tokens":0,"total_tokens":3233},{"node"